Version 2.0.1
Date: 09-09-2026

New Features:
- True Application Uninstallation Detection & Support Reporting:
    * Triggers support email ONLY upon actual application uninstallation (Inno Setup uninstaller lifecycle).
    * Offline queueing: If internet is unavailable during uninstall, records event to persistent storage and configures a background scheduled task to automatically deliver once connectivity is restored.
    * Guaranteed exactly one support email per uninstallation event with automatic queue and task cleanup.
    * Strict isolation: Internet disconnections, heartbeats, app crashes, or system restarts NEVER trigger an uninstall alert.
    * Full context payload: User ID, Username, Company, Device ID, Hostname, OS, App Version, and Uninstall Date/Time.
- Idle duration is now sent to the backend in the window_title field for idle
  sessions, matching the value displayed on the Dashboard.
- "Last successful sync" label added to the Dashboard status section.

Improvements:
- Login API payload updated to match actual backend requirements:
    * imei_number is always sent as an empty string (desktop has no IMEI).
    * os_type is dynamically detected as 'window' on Windows (singular lowercase matching CI4 API contract) and 'macos' on macOS.
    * device_detail is dynamically detected from machine BIOS/hardware (Manufacturer & Model).
- Dashboard "Tracking & Sync Status" cleaned up:
    * Removed "API Sync: Sent" row (redundant).
    * Removed "Last successful API sync" row; renamed to "Last successful sync".
- Removed and permanently hidden the "Stop Tracking" button and manual stop controls from the UI and system tray for all users. Tracking is automatically managed by system/RBAC logic and automatically resumes upon login, startup, and auto-update restarts.
- Installer shortcut permission issue fixed (PrivilegesRequired=lowest).
- Embedded Python EXE startup issue resolved.
- Device validation no longer relies on a hardcoded IMEI/device-ID retry loop.

Bug Fixes:
- Fixed "Either Duplicate Device Or Invalid Device" error by aligning dynamic os_type to 'window' as required by the backend login API.
- Fixed stale device-ID candidate list being iterated on every login attempt.
- Fixed window_title carrying the previous active-app title into idle records
  sent to the API.
- Fixed dashboard sync-error branch writing to a removed label.
- Fixed Seqrite Endpoint Protection "Trusted Email Client" popup by replacing
  direct SMTP socket connections from desktop EXE with backend HTTP API dispatch
  and local file logging fallback.
- Fixed API Sync failure details capturing (HTTP status, error responses, and
  network timeouts) to prevent generic error displays and enable safe retry.
- Fixed pre-update pending data flush session detection, lock acquisition, and
  SessionStore fallback so 0-pending update proceeds immediately and pending data
  is safely preserved without data loss during server interruptions.
- Fixed Full Auto-Update Flow with Zero Data Loss and Seamless Session Restoration:
    * Background non-blocking update check and streaming download.
    * Guaranteed pre-update data flush (activities & screenshots) before installer launch.
    * Silent Inno Setup execution & single-instance lock file clearance.
    * Automatic restart with encrypted SessionStore and ApiConfig restoration (NO re-login required).
    * Tracking automatically resumes if active before update, or remains stopped if manually stopped.
    * Startup loop prevention guard with 24-hour cooldown on repeated installation failures.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Version 2.0.0
Date: 01-09-2026

New Features:
- Automatic application update system with force-update support.
- Tracking resumes automatically after application restart (session persistence).
- Company Code verification flow added to the login screen (two-step login).
- Dynamic RBAC / permission flags pushed from server (tracking, logout, device).
- Device enrollment via enroll_device API on first login.
- Secure encrypted session storage across restarts.
- System tray with live tracking controls and status.
- Dashboard "Tracking & Sync Status" section with live counters.
- Activity batch sync with pagination (batches of 25 records per request).
- Screenshot capture on window switch and on custom interval.
- Idle detection with configurable threshold (fetched from server settings).
- Per-user activity isolation (multi-user support on shared machines).
- Windows startup (auto-launch with system) support.
- AppController endpoint for resolving company-specific API base URL.
- Version check API integration (check_new_version) after login.

Improvements:
- Replaced hardcoded API URLs with company-code-resolved base URL.
- Sync interval and idle threshold fetched dynamically from server each cycle.
- Activity records deduplicated and sorted before submission.
- Idle session idle_seconds accumulated correctly across multiple idle periods
  within the same application session.
- Single-instance guard using QLockFile to prevent duplicate background
  processes conflicting on the SQLite database.
- Sleep/resume handled: idle duration spanning system sleep is discarded.

Bug Fixes:
- Fixed activity sessions not closing correctly on application switch.
- Fixed duplicate device enrollment on re-login.
- Fixed screenshot not being associated with the correct server session ID.
- Fixed settings not persisting across restarts when DB write failed.

